content.custom_kernel_and_graphics_stack:
The operating system incorporates a customized Linux kernel (`kernel-nobara`) built with specialized patches:

- Low-latency scheduling optimizations derived from the Zen and Liquorix kernel projects;
- Fsync (`futex2`) system call synchronization patches designed to reduce CPU overhead in Wine and Proton;
- Hardware drivers for ASUS ROG gaming laptops and OpenRGB lighting controllers;
- Mesa graphics drivers compiled with hardware-accelerated video decoding/encoding (H.264, H.265, VC-1) enabled via VA-API/VDPAU;
- Out-of-the-box proprietary NVIDIA driver installation with Wayland explicit synchronization support.

content.desktop_editions_kde_and_gnome:
Nobara offers multiple desktop experiences across dedicated ISO images:

- Official Edition: The flagship desktop featuring a customized KDE Plasma 6 environment configured with an ergonomic bottom taskbar, system monitor widgets, and gaming presets;
- GNOME Edition: An alternative edition featuring GNOME with curated extensions (AppIndicator, Dash to Panel) for users who prefer GNOME workflows;
- KDE Edition: A standard, uncustomized ('stock') KDE Plasma desktop;
- Steam-Handheld & Steam-HTPC Editions: Specialized images tailored for handheld PC gaming devices (Steam Deck, ASUS ROG Ally, Lenovo Legion Go) and living room PCs, booting directly into Valve's Gamescope session ('Deck Mode').

content.gaming_and_streaming_integration:
Nobara provides a preconfigured gaming and streaming stack upon first boot:

- Steam preinstalled with complete 32-bit multilib dependency resolution;
- Pre-integrated Proton-GE, Wine-GE, and the ProtonUp-Qt management tool;
- Lutris, Heroic Games Launcher, and GOverlay preconfigured for third-party game libraries;
- MangoHud overlay for real-time monitoring of frame rates, frame times, GPU/CPU thermals, and power consumption;
- OBS Studio preconfigured with Wayland PipeWire screen capture, NVENC/VA-API hardware encoding, and GStreamer plugins;
- DaVinci Resolve compatibility libraries pre-bundled for professional video editing.

content.nobara_updater_and_welcome:
To prevent package manager conflicts resulting from manual DNF upgrades across mixed repositories, Nobara provides dedicated maintenance applications:

- `Update System` (`nobara-updater`): A specialized graphical utility that synchronizes GPG keys, coordinates system RPM updates, updates Flatpak runtimes, and applies automated post-update migration scripts;
- `Nobara Welcome`: A first-run wizard guiding users through the one-click installation of proprietary codecs, graphics drivers, and optional gaming software.

content.security_selinux_and_secure_boot:
Nobara adjusts security configurations to prioritize game compatibility:

- SELinux Permissive Mode: Unlike Fedora which enforces strict SELinux policies (`Enforcing`), Nobara sets SELinux to `Permissive` by default. This prevents game anti-cheat modules, custom Wine runtime injects, and mod loaders from being blocked by access-control denials;
- Secure Boot Requirement: Nobara does **not** support UEFI Secure Boot out of the box. Users are required to disable Secure Boot in their motherboard UEFI settings before installation, as the custom Nobara kernel and akmods drivers are not signed by Microsoft's 3rd Party UEFI Certificate Authority.

content.hardware_support_and_handhelds:
Nobara targets 64-bit `x86_64` (amd64) hardware architectures exclusively. Recommended specifications include:

- Processor: Quad-core 64-bit CPU (Intel Core i5/i7 or AMD Ryzen);
- Memory (RAM): Minimum 8 GB RAM (16 GB recommended for modern 3D gaming and content creation);
- Storage: Minimum 50 GB of disk space (SSD recommended for fast game loading);
- GPU: Dedicated AMD Radeon, NVIDIA GeForce, or Intel Arc GPU supporting Vulkan 1.3.
